From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:20:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] lab: an extender on a wired backhaul never connects its station

A lab extender whose backhaul is its LAN port (bridged into the
controller's LAN) must never connect its backhaul station: that would be
a second path into the LAN, an L2 loop. Until now the lab kept the
station away from every other mesh node on the medium, which also kept
the extender from ever being a Wi-Fi extender's backhaul parent. And
each connect attempt from OneWifi closed the extender's root admission
first, taking its own backhaul BSSs down to children, though it could
never root itself over Wi-Fi.

With /nvram/lab_wired_backhaul present (meta-cmf gen/wired-extender.sh
sets it), wifi_hal_connect refuses a mesh station before the root
admission closes: the backhaul station never associates and the
extender's backhaul BSSs stay open, so it can be a parent on the medium.
Every other extender is unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [lab]
---
 wifi_hal.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

--- a/wifi_hal.c
+++ b/wifi_hal.c
@@ -53,6 +53,8 @@
 #define MAC_ADDRESS_LEN 6
 
 #define EASYMESH_OFF_FLAG "/nvram/rdkb_user_easymesh_off"
+/* set in a lab extender whose backhaul is its LAN port (meta-cmf gen/wired-extender.sh) */
+#define LAB_WIRED_BACKHAUL_FLAG "/nvram/lab_wired_backhaul"
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_WIFI_EMULATOR
 #define RADIO_INDEX_ASSERT_RC(radioIndex, retcode) \
@@ -1445,6 +1447,16 @@
         return WIFI_HAL_INVALID_ARGUMENTS;    // RDKB-45724 - Returns -4 when the ap index is not suitable for station mode
     }
 
+    /* A lab extender on a wired backhaul (its LAN port a port of the controller's LAN)
+     * must never connect its backhaul station: that would be a second path into the
+     * LAN, an L2 loop. Refuse before the root admission closes, so its own backhaul
+     * BSSs stay open to the Wi-Fi extenders that take it as their parent. */
+    if (is_wifi_hal_vap_mesh_sta(ap_index) && access(LAB_WIRED_BACKHAUL_FLAG, F_OK) == 0) {
+        wifi_hal_info_print("%s:%d: vap index %d: wired backhaul (%s), no station connect\n",
+            __func__, __LINE__, ap_index, LAB_WIRED_BACKHAUL_FLAG);
+        return RETURN_ERR;
+    }
+
     if (is_wifi_hal_vap_mesh_sta(ap_index) &&
         wifi_hal_backhaul_root_close(ap_index) != RETURN_OK) return RETURN_ERR;
 
